)BODY
@HELP: Commands -- PRINT                        !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}  PRINT writes the log, or output, to a print file: SYSOUT or a data set.
}
@  PRINT OPEN}[class] [copies] [forms]
}    Opens SYSOUT. Without a class, it goes with your session's output.
}    PRINT OPENED; if a file is open already: PRINT ALREADY OPEN.
@  PRINT ODSN}dsname [volser or *] [OLD, SHR or MOD]
}    Opens a cataloged data set, or the one on volser. Its name is taken
}    as typed, with no prefix added. OLD writes it anew, MOD adds to it.
@  PRINT}first last
}    Prints the lines first to last: on the log, those line numbers; on
}    output, the lines of the whole output. Opens SYSOUT if no file is.
@  PRINT
}    On output, prints all of it. Elsewhere it only opens SYSOUT.
@  PRINT CLOSE
}    Closes the file: PRINT CLOSED and the lines printed. SYSOUT is then
}    printed. A file still open when SDSF ends is closed then.
}
}
}
}
